<Legal title="Privacy policy" h1="Privacy" description="How Arcus collects, uses and protects information on usearcus.ai and in our service." path="/privacy">
  <p>This policy explains what we collect when you visit usearcus.ai, fill in a form, or work with us, and what we do with it. In short: we collect what we need to answer you and improve the site, we don’t sell it, and you can ask us to delete it.</p>
  <h2 id="collect">What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>What you give us:</b> your name, work email, brand, role and anything you write or upload in a form.</li>
    <li><b>How you use the site:</b> pages viewed, buttons clicked and how you arrived (for example, an ad or a link), through product analytics. Before you accept cookies, this runs without storing anything on your device.</li>
    <li><b>Company-level visitor identification:</b> if you accept all cookies, we may use a service that matches your IP address to the company you work for. It identifies companies, not people.</li>
    <li><b>Advertising pixels:</b> if you accept all cookies, Meta and LinkedIn may measure whether our ads led to visits or sign-ups.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2 id="use">How we use it</h2>
  <ul><li>To answer your question and reply to you</li><li>To send The Receipts, if you subscribed. Every email has an unsubscribe link</li><li>To see which pages help people, and fix the ones that don’t</li><li>To measure our own ads</li></ul>
  <h2 id="client-data">Client data</h2>
  <p>Data you connect when you try Arcus free or work with us is handled as our <a href="/security">Security</a> page describes. Questions about it go to <a href="mailto:hello@usearcus.ai">hello@usearcus.ai</a>.</p>
  <h2 id="choices">Your choices</h2>
  <ul><li>Change cookie choices any time with “Cookie settings” in the footer.</li><li>We honor Global Privacy Control signals as a request to opt out of sale and sharing.</li><li>Ask to see, correct or delete your information: email <a href="mailto:hello@usearcus.ai">hello@usearcus.ai</a>.</li></ul>
  <h2 id="california">Your privacy choices (California)</h2>
  <p>California residents can ask what we collect, ask us to delete it, and opt out of “sharing” for cross-context advertising. Use Cookie settings and choose “Only necessary,” or email <a href="mailto:hello@usearcus.ai">hello@usearcus.ai</a>. We don’t sell personal information.</p>
  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy or your information go to Arcus at <a href="mailto:hello@usearcus.ai">hello@usearcus.ai</a>.</p>
</Legal>
